First, recall the formula for the perimeter of a rectangle: $P = 2 \times (length + width)$. We are given $P = 108$ cm and $length = 53$ cm. Substituting these values: $108 = 2 \times (53 + width)$. Divide both sides by 2 to get $54 = 53 + width$. Solving for the width gives $width = 54 - 53 = 1$ cm.

Next, calculate the area using the formula $Area = length \times width$. Plugging in our values: $Area = 53 \times 1 = 53$. The area is 53 square centimeters.

