The volume of the cone is $V_{cone} = \frac{1}{3}\pi r_{cone}^2 h$. Given $r_{cone} = 106$ and $h = 53$, substitute these values: $V_{cone} = \frac{1}{3}\pi (106)^2 (53)$. Note that $106 = 2 \times 53$, so $V_{cone} = \frac{1}{3}\pi (2 \cdot 53)^2 (53) = \frac{1}{3}\pi (4 \cdot 53^2) (53) = \frac{4}{3}\pi (53^3)$.

The volume of the sphere is $V_{sphere} = \frac{4}{3}\pi r_{sphere}^3$. Since the volumes are equal, set $\frac{4}{3}\pi r_{sphere}^3 = \frac{4}{3}\pi (53^3)$. Dividing both sides by $\frac{4}{3}\pi$ gives $r_{sphere}^3 = 53^3$. Taking the cube root, we find $r_{sphere} = 53$.

