First, calculate the percentage of the drink that is grape juice. The total must equal 100%. We know orange juice is 20% and watermelon juice is 27%. So, the grape juice percentage is 100% - 20% - 27% = 53%.

Next, convert this percentage into ounces based on the total volume of 100 ounces. Since 53% of 100 ounces is simply 53, the amount of grape juice is 53 ounces.

