First, use Mackenzie's purchase to find the cost of a new CD. She bought 3 new and 8 used CDs for \$70. Since one used CD costs \$5, the 8 used CDs cost $8 \times 5 = \$40$. Subtracting this from her total, the 3 new CDs cost $70 - 40 = \$30$. Thus, one new CD costs $30 / 3 = \$10$.

Next, determine how many used CDs Lakota bought. She bought 6 new CDs, costing $6 \times 10 = \$60$. Her total was \$325, so the used CDs cost $325 - 60 = \$265$. Since each used CD is \$5, she bought $265 / 5 = 53$ used compact disks.

