First, calculate the total cost of the sweets. 14 candies at $0.50 each cost $14 \times 0.5 = 7$. 20 jelly beans at $0.20 each cost $20 \times 0.2 = 4$. The total expense is $7 + 4 = 11$. Since she has $158 left after spending $11, her total money available was $158 + 11 = 169$.

Let $m$ be the amount her mother gave. Her father gave twice that, or $2m$. Including her initial $10, the equation is $10 + m + 2m = 169$. Simplifying, $10 + 3m = 169$, so $3m = 159$. Dividing by 3 gives $m = 53$. Her mother gave her $53.

