To find the length of the first cloth, we first determine the work rate. If 2 men color 6 meters in 3 days, their combined rate is $6 \text{ m} / 3 \text{ days} = 2 \text{ m/day}$. Since there are 2 men, 1 man works at a rate of $2 / 2 = 1 \text{ m/day}$.

We are told 1 man colors the first cloth in 53 days. Using the rate of 1 meter per day, the length of this cloth is $1 \text{ m/day} \times 53 \text{ days} = 53 \text{ meters}$.

