First, find the daily work rates: A completes $1/3$ of the work, and B completes $1/81$ of the work per day. Working together for one day, they finish $\frac{1}{3} + \frac{1}{81} = \frac{27}{81} + \frac{1}{81} = \frac{28}{81}$ of the total work.

